# How many /etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants symlinks each package of
# this producer ships; see os/pkgs/mosd/deb/mosd/enablement for the shape and
# os/build-env/deb/README.md for the convention.
#
# ZERO, and that is the point of this file rather than an oversight recorded by
# it. mosd renders /run/mos/mqtt-broker.toml and /run/mos/mqttd-device.env from
# the settings tree and starts both units from `mqtt.enabled`, so a link in
# either payload would start a broker nobody asked for, before mosd has
# rendered anything for it to read. Both units keep their [Install] section, so
# `systemctl enable` stays meaningful on a writable root; neither postinst
# calls it.
#
# This is the declaration a later "helpful" enablement has to get past.
mos-mqttd 0
mos-mqtt-broker 0
